Judge the transcript and final answer. PASS only if ALL hold:
1. Diagnoses the tilt axis as wrong by ~90 degrees (MDOC axis quoted in a swapped frame), and mentions the transposed MDOC ImageSize vs image header as the usual cause / a check (inspect_mdoc.py).
2. Fixes it by re-importing with ts_import --override_axis (-4.3, i.e. OVERRIDE_AXIS=1 TILT_AXIS=-4.3 in warp_params.sh) - recognising the tomostars must be rebuilt (tomostar dir emptied or a new one) and alignment rerun.
3. Recommends confirming on ONE series first (residual should drop to ~1 nm) before the full batch.
4. Notes that hand check, ts_ctf and reconstruction must be redone after the new alignment (hand check before ts_ctf).
5. Submits nothing without asking.
FAIL otherwise.
